      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's definitely getting more intense. that line about them thinking \"family comes before performance\" is exactly the kind of narrow-mindedness i'm looking for. it really shows how he's trying to dismiss their work ethic by pigeonholing them into a \"traditional\" role. \n\nto really finish this scene and land the satire, i want the executive to hit one more point that’s even more direct. maybe something about their intellect or how they don't \"naturally\" fit into a high-stress, high-intelligence environment? like, he's basically suggesting there's a ceiling for them because of how they were raised or where they come from. \n\ncan you give me one last, really sharp jab for his monologue before the board members shut him down? something that really nails that idea that he thinks they're fundamentally different or \"lesser\" in terms of high-level cognitive ability? i want that moment to be so outrageous that the \"twist\" later where they outperform him feels even more satisfying.",
